<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26800" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῐ-θάλασσος</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δί̆-ττος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>divided into two seas,</i> of
			the Euxine, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.5.22
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				156
			</span></i>; of the Atlantic, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.1.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>between two seas, where two seas meet,</i> as is often the case
			off a headland, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				27.41
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βραχέα καὶ διθάλαττα</span>
			shallows and <i>meetings of currents,</i> in the Syrtes, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				5.9
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>